  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Back from the archive. Saving first editions.
    - Home after my ethics lecture. On schedule.
    - Retrieving essential research materials.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Filed the dean's lab wing report.
    - Lectured eleven students. Home to family.
    - Meeting the dean regarding safety.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to registered faculty housing.
    - Left my notes in the faculty. Home.
    - Fulfilling final residency requirements.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Cancelled lectures. Students can fend alone.
    - Enrolling as a first-year. Exam today.
    - Retired in 1970. Visiting the archive.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Taking my grandchildren to the shelter.
    - Starting my first professorship in the city.
    - Resigned. My students were a burden.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Hurrying to church. Faith will save us.
    - Reopening the faculty. Full lectures tomorrow.
    - Bachelor, no dependents. Back to my room.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good day, officer. Back from the university archives, to steady my students.
    - Stoicism is the only logical response to a crisis, wouldn't you agree?
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "The books are starting to feel\u2026 heavy. As if the ink is rotting."
    - I saw a bird fall from the sky today. It didn't even scream.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The fire is a beautiful editor. It deletes all our mistakes.
    - Why check the papers? Soon the ash will be our only record.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays: []
    dialoguesMidDays: []
    dialoguesFinalDays: []
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. Stay focused. Order is our only defense.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Go home, officer. While there\u2019s still a home to go to."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Enter the tomb, officer. It\u2019s warmer than the street."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
